0.42: Improve the green zenith line visibility. Draw a second parallel pixel line for a slightly thicker appearance, and extend the line from the red observer point to a radial endpoint at Moon orbit + half the Moon radius. Keep V0.41 lunar clipping performance changes; use app42.js for fresh delivery.
0.41: Optimize the V0.40 Moon without changing its intended appearance. Reuse the Moon orbital unit vectors already implied by moonData(), cache the +1 px far-side erase arc at startup, remove redraw-time sqrt/division and farScale math, and build the hidden/visible lunar arcs in one loop. Use app41.js for fresh delivery.
0.40: Hide the lunar far-side outline as well as its interior. Erase the Earth-far semicircle slightly beyond the lunar radius to remove residual rim/orbit pixels, then draw only the Earth-facing semicircular limb. Keep the 0.39 far-side orientation and +10.5-day tap step; use app40.js for fresh delivery.
0.39: Add a black lunar far hemisphere. After drawing the yellow sunward and navy anti-sun illumination, overlay the half of the Moon facing away from Earth in black; this far-side orientation rotates with the Moon around Earth. Keep the 0.38 +10.5-day development tap step and use app39.js for fresh delivery.
0.38: Add a development-only in-RAM virtual clock. Each tap advances +10 days 12 hours; solar geometry, sunrise/sunset rays, Earth seasonal lighting, Moon position, and header date/time all use the same virtual time. Relaunch resets to real time. Use app38.js for fresh delivery.
0.37: Replace the single magenta tangent with two sunrise/sunset rays at ±H0 from the observer radial direction, where cos(H0)=-tan(latitude)tan(solar declination). Use shared configured lat/lon, suppress rise/set rays during polar day/night, and keep the seasonal Earth terminator driven by the same solar declination. Use app37.js for fresh delivery.
0.36: Force a fresh app payload through app36.js, keep battery number-only/right-aligned/native 12x20 behavior, add 1 px overdraw to match the clock weight, blink it with the colon while charging, and show V036 on-screen for delivery verification.
0.35: Remove battery %, right-align the numeric charge in 12x20, use green normally and red at 20% or below, and blink the battery synchronously with the time colon while charging. Narrow the date/hour separator only enough to reserve three-digit battery width.
0.34: Set minimum Moon orbit radius to Earth radius + 2×Moon radius, giving one Moon-radius of surface clearance, extend orbit support to 80 px, and position the Sun using the corona outer radius so all rays remain visible.
0.33: Add configurable Earth 25–50 px, Moon 4–15 px, Moon orbit 40–70 px and Sun 4–15 px. Automatically place Earth so the Moon envelope touches the left/bottom edges, place Sun against the right/header boundary, and enforce a non-overlap minimum Moon orbit.
0.32: Finish the Moon with navy shadow and vivid-yellow sunward hemisphere, read Moon radius 3–15 px from shared settings, and restore the Earth-center to Sun-center reference line underneath the bodies.
0.31: Replace phase-shape Moon filling with a cached illuminated semicircle aligned to the Earth-to-Sun direction, modeling parallel sunlight from a distant Sun at every lunar orbit position. This also removes the costly per-redraw phase polygon math.
0.30: Precompute Moon cross-section sqrt values at startup and reduce phase-boundary samples from 17 to 9, preserving the 7 px Moon appearance while reducing the M redraw cost.
0.29: Enlarge M/H/T diagnostics from 4x6 to 6x8 below the header; keep lunar age on a smaller second line. Moon phase drawing is unchanged.
0.28: Add lightweight Moon phase shading and move diagnostics from the bottom edge to a compact line below the header so the lunar orbit remains unobstructed.
0.27: Add the Moon orbit and current lunar-age position only. New Moon is placed toward the Sun and the Moon moves around Earth with the synodic cycle; phase shading is deferred. Add M timing.
0.26: Reduce seasonal terminator points from 13 to 7 and cache the fixed Sun-direction basis, projected base points and anti-solar limb, minimizing per-redraw geometry while preserving the curved seasonal boundary.
0.25: Cache all sqrt(R^2-v^2) terminator span values at startup and reuse them on redraw, preserving the 0.24 seasonal terminator appearance while reducing floating-point cost.
0.24: Use current solar declination to draw a curved north-polar day/night terminator and vary the illuminated fraction seasonally; keep the 0.23 header and observer path unchanged.
